From 626cd4e0ce575987dcbcebd27c6a9f1939cbdc3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fieldmar <974888+fieldmar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:03:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] camellia: disable ViLTE so the modem brings up IMS

With video calling (ViLTE) enabled for a SIM, the RIL sends
AT+EIMSCFG=1,1,... and the modem never requests the IMS PDN
(+EIMSPDN "notify" never arrives), so VoLTE never registers.
With ViLTE off it sends AT+EIMSCFG=1,0,... as stock MIUI does, and
IMS registers on EE and Three; VoLTE calls work both ways.

The Settings "Video calling" switch defaults to on and does not
reliably save off, so turn ViLTE support off for the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I56862a3f588c234ae06fd30801b68439cf22693b
---
 vendor.prop | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vendor.prop b/vendor.prop
index 98be728..447ae1c 100644
--- a/vendor.prop
+++ b/vendor.prop
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ persist.vendor.mtk.volte.enable=1
 persist.vendor.mtk_ct_volte_support=3
 persist.vendor.mtk_dynamic_ims_switch=1
 persist.vendor.mtk_wfc_support=1
-persist.vendor.vilte_support=1
+persist.vendor.vilte_support=0
 persist.vendor.viwifi_support=1
 persist.vendor.volte_support=1
 persist.vendor.vonr_setting_support=1
-- 
